WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.330
- Well, we've found one of
your first casting shots.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.380
Let's put it up here.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:06.790
This,
(laughing)

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:08.610
this is like rock and roll.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.970
Like this is like, is this
your Joan Jett, The Cure?

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.640
There's so many things
happening, I love it.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.610
So did you get any work from these shots?

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.280
- So.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.460
Look, my agent at the time was
like, we need some pictures.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.790
I was like, sure.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.623
You know,

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:26.910
I was like rolling with
whatever people were telling me.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.580
I was like, this is gonna be great.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:30.230
Obviously I wasn't auditioning

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.780
to be in boy bands at the time,

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:32.680
so it didn't help me

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.700
get any work,
(audience laughs)

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.790
but I got to use the sauna at the hotel,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.170
so I got like a nice spa day from it.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.610
- I think you look cool.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.860
I think from that picture though,

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.990
I was like, I would've
pegged you as a musician,

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.320
not an actor.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:48.780
I was like, she definitely

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.625
plays music.
- Yeah, but also

00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:52.997
I sent a selfie to someone
yesterday and they were like,

00:00:52.997 --> 00:00:55.144
"Oh, I thought that was Harry Styles."

00:00:55.144 --> 00:00:56.410
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:57.330
- Well, he's gorgeous.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.280
See, you're even pretty as a boy.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.040
So, you don't actually have the force,

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.860
or maybe you do and you're hiding it.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:05.973
But is it true that you
do have a witchy sense?

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:07.993
- Yes.

00:01:07.993 --> 00:01:10.600
People say I have, witchy senses,

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.340
I'm quite, I think they call them USP,

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:14.840
ultra sensitive person, right?

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:20.320
I tend to be able to read
people's moods quite well

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.290
to a point that people
comment on it often.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.493
- Oh, you're an empath.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:27.755
Like you're kind of,
- Yeah.

00:01:27.755 --> 00:01:30.250
But I think everyone sort of is,

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.870
if they will open to it,

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:35.333
I just think I'm quite
watchful, so I notice things.

00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:37.504
But yes, an empath, I guess.

00:01:37.504 --> 00:01:38.980
- I am like that.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.920
That's why everybody makes
fun of me because I cry a lot.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:41.820
And I'm like,

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.360
I feel what everyone's feeling.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.900
Like if someone's nervous,

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.100
if someone is angry,

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.660
I am like a sponge for people's feelings.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:55.370
And I think it's kind of nice
because you, I don't know,

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:56.980
I think it makes you an empathetic person,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:58.490
so you can put yourself
in someone's shoes easily,

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:01.340
but at the same time, it's
kind of, it's exhausting.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:02.350
So yeah.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.290
- It is exhausting.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.860
And I think on the question
of the Chaos Walking too,

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.907
I already find it tiring
enough when I'm like

00:02:07.907 --> 00:02:10.900
dealing with my own
neuroses as we all have.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.780
And then like you're picking
up on other people's moods

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.180
and you're being affected by that.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.870
Like, if you were to have that next level

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:18.270
and hear people's thoughts,
like that's heavy.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.290
I don't want that on my shoulders.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:21.123
- Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:02:21.123 --> 00:02:22.040
Was there ever a moment,

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.510
like you felt like it was too much

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.310
when you were around
someone and you were like,

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.610
ooh, you could feel it so much

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.861
that you just had to tell them?

00:02:28.861 --> 00:02:31.350
- Hm, I don't think so.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:35.020
But I will tell you the,
on the subject of senses,

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.600
'cause it's not just
senses with other people,

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.220
there was this joke that
I went whale watching

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.357
and I went, "Ooh!"

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.449
and a whale came out of the sea.

00:02:44.449 --> 00:02:45.550
(audience laughs)
- [Kelly] What?

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:47.833
- I'm not joking, yeah, yeah.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:51.460
- Okay, so one time I
was on a safari in Africa

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.310
and it was like our first time

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.590
and we were in the truck

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.730
and we literally headed out the gates

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.130
in Sabi Sands in Kruger National Park,

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.820
And I was like, "Queue the lion."

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:05.980
And like literally
within like five minutes,

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:08.270
I spotted a female lion

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:10.960
that led us to like a whole pride of lions

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.070
with baby lions, little cubs.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.560
And then they stole and ate Paula's food.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.376
And I was like, that
was rude, but whatever.

00:03:16.376 --> 00:03:18.770
But no, I've done something like that.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:20.040
That's amazing though.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.110
So you're kind of like Nemo as well.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:23.740
You do have superpowers.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.760
I like it.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.400
Well, since you're from London,
I have to ask you about,

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.570
you know, British pub life.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.810
I love a British pub, by the by,

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.863
but have you ever worked at the pub?

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.570
- Yes, I've worked at two.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.946
One, not so fun,

00:03:39.946 --> 00:03:41.240
was a bit of a drag.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.790
The second, really enjoyed it.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.900
And they had a five pound
burger on a Wednesday.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:45.760
So it was always great,

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.070
'cause we always got a
burger when we were working.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:49.910
- That's amazing, that's a big burger.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:51.160
That's very Texan of you.

